+## Indexes
+
+Register an index and the planner will use it where it can:
+
+```python
+session.create_index("orders", "customer_id")
+session.create_index("orders", "ordered_on", kind="sorted")
+
+session.sql("SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id IN (1, 5)")   # hash lookup
+session.sql("SELECT * FROM orders ORDER BY ordered_on")           # no sort at all
+```
+
+Indexes are a speed decision and nothing more: the rows that come back, and
+the order they come back in, are exactly what the same query returns without
+them. `SHOW INDEXES` says what the catalog holds.
+
